/**
 * @addtogroup Foundation_BuildGuide_SupportMatrix
 *
 * This page defines the support evidence for the Foundation 1.x release line.
 * Foundation 1.2.0 is the current published release. A preset being
 * present in `CMakePresets.json` proves that a build identity is described; it
 * does not by itself prove that its compiler, package, consumer, or target
 * execution has been validated.
 *
 * @section FoundationSupportMatrixLevels Support Levels
 *
 * | Level | Meaning |
 * | ----- | ------- |
 * | `PUBLISHED` | A package for this exact target identity was produced from a version tag and passed native tests plus the standalone package consumer. |
 * | `RELEASE CANDIDATE` | Intended to become supported in the 1.x line, but its required validation remains incomplete. |
 * | `SUPPORTED` | All applicable release gates passed on the released commit and Foundation commits to maintaining that target for the 1.x line. |
 * | `EXPERIMENTAL` | Preset or integration is available for evaluation, but compatibility is best effort. |
 * | `DEFERRED` | Explicitly outside the current 1.x scope. No release package or compatibility promise is made. |
 * | `INTERNAL` | Repository workflow infrastructure, not a consumer platform or distributed binary identity. |
 *
 * `PUBLISHED` records verifiable package delivery; it does not grant license
 * rights or claim hardware validation. A `RELEASE CANDIDATE` or `PUBLISHED` row
 * becomes `SUPPORTED` only when its validation task
 * in @ref Foundation_Workflows_ReleaseV1 is `DONE`. If that evidence cannot be
 * completed, the row remains explicitly limited; it must not silently become a
 * broader support claim.
 *
 * @section FoundationSupportMatrixDesktop Native Desktop Targets
 *
 * Native targets must compile and run the non-zero GoogleTest suite in Debug
 * and Release, export a Release-only package, run applicable examples, and link
 * a separate package consumer.
 *
 * | Platform | Preset | Compiler / architecture | 1.x level | Validation gate |
 * | -------- | ------ | ----------------------- | ---------- | --------------- |
 * | macOS | `macos_arm64` | Apple Clang, arm64 | `PUBLISHED` | VAL-001 |
 * | macOS | `macos_x64` | Apple Clang, x86-64 | `RELEASE CANDIDATE` | VAL-002 |
 * | Windows | `windows_msvc_x64` | MSVC, x86-64 | `PUBLISHED` | VAL-003 |
 * | Windows | `windows_clang_x64` | Clang, x86-64 | `PUBLISHED` | VAL-004 |
 * | Linux | `linux_gcc_x64` | GCC, x86-64 | `PUBLISHED` | VAL-005 |
 * | Linux | `linux_clang_x64` | Clang, x86-64 | `PUBLISHED` | VAL-005 |
 * | Linux | `linux_gcc_arm64` | GCC, AArch64 | `RELEASE CANDIDATE` | VAL-006 |
 * | Linux | `linux_clang_arm64` | Clang, AArch64 | `RELEASE CANDIDATE` | VAL-006 |
 *
 * `macos_x64` may be cross-built on Apple Silicon, but execution still requires
 * Rosetta or Intel hardware. Linux Arm64 requires a native Arm64 runner or
 * Raspberry Pi-class host; an x86-64 container is not equivalent evidence.
 *
 * @section FoundationSupportMatrixEmbedded Named Embedded Targets
 *
 * Embedded support has separate compile/package and execution evidence. A
 * successful archive build is necessary but not sufficient: the exported
 * package must link into firmware built with the same compiler, CPU, ABI, and
 * FPU settings. Representative hardware or an appropriate emulator provides
 * the behavioral evidence.
 *
 * | Platform | Preset / integration | Binary identity | 1.x level | Validation gate |
 * | -------- | -------------------- | --------------- | ---------- | --------------- |
 * | AVR | `atmega328p_avrgcc_avr5` | AVR-GCC, ATmega328P, AVR5 | `RELEASE CANDIDATE` | VAL-007 |
 * | STM32F103 | `stm32f103_armgcc_cortex_m3_soft` | Arm GCC, Cortex-M3, soft float | `RELEASE CANDIDATE` | VAL-008 |
 * | STM32F407 | `stm32f407_armgcc_cortex_m4f_hard` | Arm GCC, Cortex-M4F, hard float | `RELEASE CANDIDATE` | VAL-008 |
 * | STM32H743 | `stm32h743_armgcc_cortex_m7f_hard` | Arm GCC, Cortex-M7F, hard float | `RELEASE CANDIDATE` | VAL-008 |
 * | PSoC 5LP | `psoc5lp_armgcc_cortex_m3_soft` | Arm GCC, Cortex-M3, soft float | `EXPERIMENTAL` | VAL-009 |
 *
 * PSoC remains experimental until its exact product toolchain and a real
 * consumer project are validated. The STM32 presets do not promise CMSIS, HAL,
 * startup files, linker scripts, device macros, or flashing support; those are
 * owned by the consuming firmware.
 *
 * @section FoundationSupportMatrixProfiles Generic Arm Profiles
 *
 * The following presets are reusable toolchain/ABI building blocks. They are
 * experimental standalone packages in the 1.x line because a CPU core alone does not
 * define a complete board, runtime, device, or firmware integration:
 *
 * | Preset | Profile | 1.x level |
 * | ------ | ------- | ---------- |
 * | `arm_none_eabi_cortex_m0plus_soft` | Cortex-M0+, soft float | `EXPERIMENTAL` |
 * | `arm_none_eabi_cortex_m3_soft` | Cortex-M3, soft float | `EXPERIMENTAL` |
 * | `arm_none_eabi_cortex_m4f_hard` | Cortex-M4F, hard float | `EXPERIMENTAL` |
 * | `arm_none_eabi_cortex_m7f_hard` | Cortex-M7F, hard float | `EXPERIMENTAL` |
 *
 * The named STM32 and PSoC presets inherit these profiles but have independent
 * support status and validation evidence.
 *
 * @section FoundationSupportMatrixSourceMode Source-Mode Integrations
 *
 * | Integration | 1.x level | Scope |
 * | ----------- | ---------- | ----- |
 * | Arduino Uno / ATmega328P source mode | `RELEASE CANDIDATE` | The documented sketches must compile with the declared Arduino AVR core. |
 * | Other Arduino cores | `EXPERIMENTAL` | Source-compatible by design, but not validated as a group. Each architecture needs explicit evidence. |
 * | Direct source inclusion in a higher-level CMake project | `EXPERIMENTAL` | The supported v1 consumer path is the exported package; source inclusion still requires a dedicated consumer contract. |
 * | PIC | `DEFERRED` | No current preset, toolchain, package, or compatibility promise. |
 *
 * @section FoundationSupportMatrixWorkflowPresets Workflow-Only Presets
 *
 * | Preset | 1.x level | Purpose |
 * | ------ | ---------- | ------- |
 * | `documentation` | `INTERNAL` | Builds Doxygen output; it is not a Foundation binary package. |
 *
 * Hidden presets such as `base`, `docs_base`, and `testing_base` are inheritance
 * implementation details and are not user-selectable compatibility targets.
 *
 * @section FoundationSupportMatrixReleaseRule Release Rule
 *
 * Each release tag freezes its support evidence. A published package may be
 * described as `PUBLISHED` only when the tagged workflow produced that exact
 * identity. Adding a compiler, architecture, ABI, MCU, or board requires its
 * own validation and a later compatible release; similarity to an existing
 * preset is not proof of support.
 */
